this morning local businesses came  together for an event showcase it's all  to network and highlight the services  available for business owners mary jane  belliesa shares why the community's  support means more amount more now than  ever  over 50 local businesses were in  attendance at the clark county  amphitheater for small business saturday  with the goal of supporting local  business owners and increasing their  opportunities for success chantal de  laurentii owns a taste of coffee she  says it's not only important to receive  community support but for other  businesses to support each other we  wouldn't be here without our locals and  so one of the things that we give back  to is we have baked goods that we  actually bring in small local businesses  one example is we have the aussie  projects that they actually make  australian meat pies in which we're  really super excited because they are  actually going to start having them in  store aussie project restaurant owner  alex biffin says partnerships like these  is a good way to reach new patrons and  make connections i've actually just  joined a group it's a bni business group  and their main their whole outlook on on  business is helping each other out and  i've sort of just really adopted that i  really love that i just love the  camaraderie and the community spirit  christina amos owner of bella natural  says while she was lucky to have built a  base of loyal customers prior to the  pandemic she knows not everyone is as  lucky so those customers kept me alive  and that was so important for me  in colton during colby times and that's  why another reason why it's so important  for the community support our small  businesses because you keep us alive  mary jane ballaza live
 

